1
00:00:19,100 --> 00:00:20,334
Why?

2
00:00:20,334 --> 00:00:22,270
Do you miss me already?

3
00:00:22,270 --> 00:00:24,005
Nero...

4
00:00:24,005 --> 00:00:25,974
we need to talk.

5
00:00:25,974 --> 00:00:28,443
How was your sleep? Was it good?

6
00:00:28,443 --> 00:00:31,012
The truth is, I didn't sleep well last night.

7
00:00:31,012 --> 00:00:33,815
I kept thinking about what Don Ferell said.

8
00:00:33,815 --> 00:00:37,051
We should know who killed Alyanna.

9
00:00:37,051 --> 00:00:39,972
Don't you remember anything, buddy? Anything.

10
00:00:39,973 --> 00:00:40,634
Just a little.

11
00:00:40,634 --> 00:00:44,525
Maybe I can remember
the shape of the head, the shape of his eyes.

12
00:00:44,525 --> 00:00:47,166
My grandfather once said...

13
00:00:47,167 --> 00:00:51,515
that if you return
to the scene of the crime...

14
00:00:52,266 --> 00:00:57,672
it might trigger
and make you remember what happened.

15
00:00:57,672 --> 00:00:58,873
Federico.

16
00:00:58,873 --> 00:01:01,576
Why don't we go back
to the scene of the crime?

17
00:01:01,576 --> 00:01:04,912
Florence, sorry, but there's trouble again.

18
00:01:04,912 --> 00:01:08,916
Hey Ferell guys, what did you do again?
This spells trouble again.

19
00:01:08,916 --> 00:01:11,919
- Surprise!
- Surprise!

20
00:01:11,919 --> 00:01:14,689
No more talking about
Florence being an Almero.

21
00:01:14,689 --> 00:01:18,926
In this space, she is just Florence.

22
00:01:18,926 --> 00:01:21,396
There are a lot of things
we need to talk about,

23
00:01:21,396 --> 00:01:23,164
like how is she and Nero.

24
00:01:23,164 --> 00:01:28,169
And what's the stage of their relationship.

25
00:01:28,169 --> 00:01:30,805
How about you, Florence? Do you have plans?

26
00:01:30,805 --> 00:01:32,807
I don't know what to answer.

27
00:01:32,807 --> 00:01:36,411
It seems for the first time in my life...

28
00:01:36,411 --> 00:01:38,146
I have no plans.

29
00:01:38,146 --> 00:01:44,018
How can you dream
if you have an influential family?

30
00:01:44,018 --> 00:01:47,237
I don't know
what kind of future is waiting for us.

31
00:01:48,322 --> 00:01:50,275
But what I only know is...

32
00:01:51,459 --> 00:01:56,002
I love you so much.

33
00:01:58,833 --> 00:02:07,942
And I love you so much too,
Nero Sebastian Araneta Ferell.

34
00:03:22,705 --> 00:03:25,268
Come on, please answer.

35
00:03:28,376 --> 00:03:31,591
<i>Sorry, the subscriber cannot be reached.</i>

36
00:03:33,594 --> 00:03:36,380
Sir, I saw this among Celestina's belongings.

37
00:03:43,359 --> 00:03:46,807
So this is the reason
why you're acting that way?

38
00:03:46,807 --> 00:03:48,843
You're still talking to him?

39
00:03:48,843 --> 00:03:51,348
Do you still allow him to brainwash you?

40
00:03:51,348 --> 00:03:55,073
You would rather believe him
than your own father?

41
00:03:59,690 --> 00:04:02,089
You are not leaving this house.

42
00:04:02,089 --> 00:04:06,794
I will fix your papers
and we will leave as soon as possible.

43
00:04:06,794 --> 00:04:08,229
- Baste?
- Sir?

44
00:04:08,229 --> 00:04:10,199
Keep an eye on her.

45
00:04:10,199 --> 00:04:12,884
I don't want her talking to someone else.

46
00:04:13,589 --> 00:04:17,208
I will not let the Ferells
turn my own child against me.

47
00:04:18,206 --> 00:04:20,190
What's happening here?

48
00:04:29,339 --> 00:04:32,625
<i>Sorry, the subscriber cannot be reached.</i>

49
00:04:37,225 --> 00:04:38,740
Nero?

50
00:04:39,615 --> 00:04:41,646
Is that Florence?

51
00:04:42,709 --> 00:04:43,866
Yes, Mother.

52
00:04:43,866 --> 00:04:47,368
Wow, you're calling her mother.
"Son-in-law" is your peg.

53
00:04:47,368 --> 00:04:51,349
If you're able to contact her,
can I talk to her too?

54
00:04:52,802 --> 00:04:54,575
That's the thing, Mother.

55
00:04:54,575 --> 00:04:56,693
She didn't answer her call.

56
00:04:58,479 --> 00:05:00,681
Maybe the battery is low.

57
00:05:00,681 --> 00:05:02,617
Or maybe she got caught.

58
00:05:02,617 --> 00:05:05,898
Maybe she got caught
talking to you guys secretly,

59
00:05:05,898 --> 00:05:08,576
that's why her father got mad
and confiscated her phone.

60
00:05:08,576 --> 00:05:10,578
Patotina, you're overreacting.

61
00:05:10,578 --> 00:05:15,416
Maybe there's no signal at home,
or her phone is turned off.

62
00:05:15,416 --> 00:05:18,255
Well Nero, if you're able to contact her,

63
00:05:18,255 --> 00:05:20,788
I want to talk to her too.

64
00:05:20,788 --> 00:05:22,123
Maybe she needs something.

65
00:05:22,123 --> 00:05:25,493
I'll just send it to the school
and you can hand it over to her.

66
00:05:25,493 --> 00:05:27,323
Okay, Mother.

67
00:05:31,766 --> 00:05:33,483
What are you doing?

68
00:05:34,535 --> 00:05:36,037
I'm trying to be a father.

69
00:05:36,037 --> 00:05:40,608
With what you're doing,
you are driving her away from us.

70
00:05:40,608 --> 00:05:42,243
So what should I do?

71
00:05:42,243 --> 00:05:43,511
She's testing me.

72
00:05:43,511 --> 00:05:47,798
She's testing my patience
when it comes to the Ferells.

73
00:05:48,516 --> 00:05:50,918
Garpidio talked to me.

74
00:05:50,918 --> 00:05:51,986
Why?

75
00:05:51,986 --> 00:05:54,288
He wanted to talk about Florence.

76
00:05:54,288 --> 00:05:56,057
Why? What does he care?

77
00:05:56,057 --> 00:05:59,327
Florence is important
to him and his grandsons,

78
00:05:59,327 --> 00:06:04,367
and he wants us
to fix the misunderstanding our family has,

79
00:06:04,367 --> 00:06:06,183
for her.

80
00:06:06,924 --> 00:06:08,703
He killed my wife.

81
00:06:08,703 --> 00:06:10,605
He killed the love of my life.

82
00:06:10,605 --> 00:06:13,241
You don't understand that either?

83
00:06:13,241 --> 00:06:15,977
We don't know that, Lorenzo!

84
00:06:15,977 --> 00:06:19,146
We felt he had something to do with Alyanna,

85
00:06:19,146 --> 00:06:21,382
but we were not able to prove anything.

86
00:06:21,382 --> 00:06:24,218
You let the Ferells fool you again?

87
00:06:24,218 --> 00:06:27,221
They are influential people here in Levante.

88
00:06:27,221 --> 00:06:29,357
Of course, they can hide their crimes.

89
00:06:29,357 --> 00:06:31,926
You know, this is my fault.

90
00:06:31,926 --> 00:06:35,396
Because I've inculcated my anger
towards Garpidio in you.

91
00:06:35,396 --> 00:06:38,332
And now, it's affecting your relationship
with your daughter.

92
00:06:38,332 --> 00:06:41,302
You know, that's the problem with you.

93
00:06:41,302 --> 00:06:43,237
You're already old,
that's why you tend to forget things,

94
00:06:43,237 --> 00:06:46,240
and as a result,
it's easy for the Ferells to fool you.

95
00:06:46,240 --> 00:06:48,309
How dare you?

96
00:06:48,309 --> 00:06:50,594
Hello, guys. What's up?

97
00:06:51,379 --> 00:06:53,163
Is everything okay?

98
00:06:54,749 --> 00:06:56,300
What do you need?

99
00:06:57,079 --> 00:06:59,731
Dad, calm down.

100
00:07:10,999 --> 00:07:14,052
<i>Sorry, the subscriber cannot be reached.</i>

101
00:07:17,605 --> 00:07:19,473
Hey, what's the problem?

102
00:07:19,473 --> 00:07:21,442
I can't contact Florence.

103
00:07:21,442 --> 00:07:23,678
Her phone has been unattended
since last night.

104
00:07:23,678 --> 00:07:25,613
Didn't we tell you that maybe she's busy?

105
00:07:25,613 --> 00:07:27,782
We designated a time to talk.

106
00:07:27,782 --> 00:07:29,083
Besides, that's supposed to be the schedule

107
00:07:29,083 --> 00:07:32,253
for her to talk to her mother and father.

108
00:07:32,253 --> 00:07:35,156
It's very unlikely of her
to miss her call appointment.

109
00:07:35,156 --> 00:07:37,058
Exactly.

110
00:07:37,058 --> 00:07:39,576
Wait, Nero is here.

111
00:07:39,576 --> 00:07:41,460
- Nero.
- Who's that?

112
00:07:41,460 --> 00:07:43,560
It's the girls. They want to talk to you.

113
00:07:46,467 --> 00:07:48,903
- <i>Nero, are you there?</i>
- Yes.

114
00:07:48,903 --> 00:07:50,604
<i>Were you able to talk to Florence?</i>

115
00:07:50,604 --> 00:07:52,573
That's what we were talking about.

116
00:07:52,573 --> 00:07:54,942
I can't contact her since last night.

117
00:07:54,942 --> 00:07:57,144
<i>She's also not here.</i>

118
00:07:57,144 --> 00:07:59,914
<i>And it's so unlikely for her
to miss this meeting.</i>

119
00:07:59,914 --> 00:08:02,650
<i>Especially since we need
the head of the Communication Arts</i>

120
00:08:02,650 --> 00:08:06,153
<i>to plan the season ender event of our school.</i>

121
00:08:06,153 --> 00:08:08,189
I'm sorry but I wasn't able to talk to her,

122
00:08:08,189 --> 00:08:10,540
and I also don't have an idea where she is.

123
00:08:11,467 --> 00:08:14,528
<i>Which makes me worry, Nero.</i>

124
00:08:14,528 --> 00:08:15,663
Why?

125
00:08:15,663 --> 00:08:17,865
<i>Well, on my way here,</i>

126
00:08:17,865 --> 00:08:21,435
<i>I overheard my dad talking
to Mr. Lorenzo Almero,</i>

127
00:08:21,435 --> 00:08:23,104
<i>Florence's dad.</i>

128
00:08:23,104 --> 00:08:25,473
<i>I heard that he was asking for my dad's help</i>

129
00:08:25,473 --> 00:08:28,743
<i>to expedite the processing
of Florence's papers.</i>

130
00:08:28,743 --> 00:08:30,244
What for?

131
00:08:30,244 --> 00:08:32,413
<i>I wasn't able to hear the complete details,</i>

132
00:08:32,413 --> 00:08:37,051
<i>but expediting travel documents
could only mean one thing.</i>

133
00:08:37,051 --> 00:08:40,888
<i>I think
the Almeros are taking Florence away from us.</i>

134
00:08:40,888 --> 00:08:45,142
<i>I think her dad is sending her
to live and study abroad.</i>

135
00:09:09,620 --> 00:09:11,310
Mr. Baste.

136
00:09:41,816 --> 00:09:46,053
And if there's a victim here, that's you.

137
00:09:46,053 --> 00:09:49,356
You're a victim of your own anger.

138
00:09:49,356 --> 00:09:52,960
You're a victim of the pain you felt
when you lost Mommy.

139
00:09:52,960 --> 00:09:53,994
Why?

140
00:09:53,994 --> 00:09:56,363
Because you weren't able to protect her.

141
00:09:56,363 --> 00:09:58,466
You failed to save her.

142
00:09:58,466 --> 00:10:00,634
That's why you're looking
for someone else to blame

143
00:10:00,634 --> 00:10:03,270
because of your own failure.

144
00:10:03,270 --> 00:10:06,373
Because you knew deep in you
that you once neglected your family.

145
00:10:06,373 --> 00:10:08,275
That's why you lost me, right?

146
00:10:08,275 --> 00:10:09,626
Enough!

147
00:10:11,245 --> 00:10:13,047
Go to your room!

148
00:10:13,047 --> 00:10:14,348
Pack your bags.

149
00:10:14,348 --> 00:10:18,153
I'm pulling you out of the university
and taking you with me to the States.

150
00:10:23,569 --> 00:10:25,193
Hi.

151
00:10:26,994 --> 00:10:28,654
Florence?

152
00:10:30,397 --> 00:10:31,841
Am I right?

153
00:10:32,933 --> 00:10:34,631
You're Florence?

154
00:10:35,404 --> 00:10:38,065
Yes, I'm Florence.

155
00:10:38,065 --> 00:10:43,426
But I think it should be Celestina,
because that's my real name.

156
00:10:44,545 --> 00:10:46,029
Celestina...

157
00:10:47,948 --> 00:10:49,650
But just between you and me,

158
00:10:49,650 --> 00:10:53,821
I think I prefer to call you Florence.

159
00:10:53,821 --> 00:10:56,920
Just like the beautiful place in Italy.

160
00:10:56,920 --> 00:10:58,514
It's Florence.

161
00:11:01,128 --> 00:11:03,254
I'm Samuel.

162
00:11:04,910 --> 00:11:07,167
Your Uncle Samuel.

163
00:11:07,167 --> 00:11:09,203
Uncle Samuel?

164
00:11:09,203 --> 00:11:10,704
Yes.

165
00:11:10,704 --> 00:11:13,575
I'm your father's brother.

166
00:11:14,341 --> 00:11:17,778
Well, we're not blood-related, but...

167
00:11:17,778 --> 00:11:21,331
your Grandpa Roger treated me as a real son.

168
00:11:22,316 --> 00:11:26,387
And there,
maybe they failed to introduce me to you,

169
00:11:26,387 --> 00:11:31,508
because they're very protective
when it comes to you.

170
00:11:33,694 --> 00:11:37,665
Is that why they practically lock me up
here in the mansion

171
00:11:37,665 --> 00:11:41,952
and force me to move to another country
even if I don't want to?

172
00:11:43,437 --> 00:11:46,404
You know, Florence, I understand you.

173
00:11:48,076 --> 00:11:52,546
And I understand the fear of a father.

174
00:11:52,546 --> 00:11:56,666
But soon, when you become a parent,
you'll understand everything.

175
00:11:57,568 --> 00:12:00,771
You'll know where your father is coming from.

176
00:12:01,822 --> 00:12:04,959
I understand him...

177
00:12:04,959 --> 00:12:08,262
and his fears.

178
00:12:08,262 --> 00:12:09,997
But...

179
00:12:09,997 --> 00:12:14,017
should we live in fear
for the rest of our lives?

180
00:12:18,023 --> 00:12:19,474
You're right.

181
00:12:20,874 --> 00:12:22,712
I understand you.

182
00:12:24,080 --> 00:12:26,231
And because I understand you...

183
00:12:28,048 --> 00:12:30,834
I can help you escape from the mansion.

184
00:12:31,716 --> 00:12:33,167
Do you want that?

185
00:12:35,856 --> 00:12:37,240
Really?

186
00:12:45,933 --> 00:12:48,669
The Almeros will bring Florence
to the States.

187
00:12:48,669 --> 00:12:50,381
Antonia overheard her dad,

188
00:12:50,381 --> 00:12:53,073
and they're expediting
the processing of her papers.

189
00:12:53,073 --> 00:12:54,708
That's unacceptable, Grandpa.

190
00:12:54,708 --> 00:12:56,443
She was excellent in school.

191
00:12:56,443 --> 00:12:58,846
Why does she have to study abroad?

192
00:12:58,846 --> 00:13:02,160
Yes, Grandpa.
Why are they sending Florence to the States?

193
00:13:02,160 --> 00:13:04,777
The discrimination against Asians
is too much there.

194
00:13:04,777 --> 00:13:05,953
We should stop this, Grandpa.

195
00:13:05,953 --> 00:13:08,389
We should take Florence back from them.

196
00:13:08,389 --> 00:13:10,924
Stop this nonsense.

197
00:13:10,924 --> 00:13:13,193
No one is going to do anything.

198
00:13:13,193 --> 00:13:16,296
We should respect the rights of the Almeros.

199
00:13:16,296 --> 00:13:17,781
Really, Grandpa?

200
00:13:18,866 --> 00:13:20,582
You'll just let them?

201
00:13:20,582 --> 00:13:22,169
You won't do anything?

202
00:13:22,169 --> 00:13:24,238
You'll just leave Florence to them?

203
00:13:24,238 --> 00:13:27,089
Nero, lower your voice.

204
00:13:27,089 --> 00:13:29,543
You're still talking to your grandfather.

205
00:13:29,543 --> 00:13:33,263
You can't always do things your way
all the time.

206
00:13:36,550 --> 00:13:38,752
I spoke to Rogelio.

207
00:13:38,752 --> 00:13:42,556
I beg him for us
to settle this thing between us,

208
00:13:42,556 --> 00:13:45,023
for Florence's sake.

209
00:13:45,023 --> 00:13:47,070
He didn't forgive me.

210
00:13:47,070 --> 00:13:48,395
He even warned me.

211
00:13:48,395 --> 00:13:51,247
He warned all of us to stay away from her.

212
00:13:53,701 --> 00:13:57,237
And Lydia, I'm sorry, I'm afraid.

213
00:13:57,237 --> 00:13:59,089
We have no choice.

214
00:13:59,740 --> 00:14:04,627
I did everything I could do, but I failed.

215
00:14:05,342 --> 00:14:06,668
So...

216
00:14:07,515 --> 00:14:10,332
Do you understand now
what your grandpa meant?

217
00:14:11,485 --> 00:14:14,788
If we keep insisting to be close to Florence,

218
00:14:14,788 --> 00:14:20,327
the conflict between the Ferells and the Almeros
can escalate.

219
00:14:20,327 --> 00:14:22,801
Florence will have a harder time.

220
00:14:22,801 --> 00:14:26,049
And the best thing we could do right now
is just to...

221
00:14:26,934 --> 00:14:28,668
let her be.

222
00:14:31,508 --> 00:14:32,167
You're saying that

223
00:14:32,167 --> 00:14:35,291
because you're not getting hurt
with everything that's happening now.

224
00:14:40,114 --> 00:14:41,849
Nero?

225
00:14:41,849 --> 00:14:44,251
Grandpa, I'll take care of him.

226
00:14:44,251 --> 00:14:45,929
Nero?

227
00:14:58,632 --> 00:15:01,889
This scrambled egg that you cooked
is delicious.

228
00:15:02,503 --> 00:15:07,290
The rumors are true.
You're a good cook, Florence.

229
00:15:08,041 --> 00:15:10,110
- Thank you.
- It's so delicious.

230
00:15:10,110 --> 00:15:12,980
I thought
I'll be able to get out of the mansion

231
00:15:12,980 --> 00:15:14,806
and you'll help me escape,

232
00:15:14,806 --> 00:15:19,153
but you just took me to the kitchen
so I can cook for you.

233
00:15:19,153 --> 00:15:21,622
It turns out you're hungry.

234
00:15:21,622 --> 00:15:22,890
I'm sorry.

235
00:15:22,890 --> 00:15:26,660
You know
that's just about what your Uncle Samuel can do.

236
00:15:26,660 --> 00:15:29,329
But I know the guards.

237
00:15:29,329 --> 00:15:32,115
You can come out of your room anytime.

238
00:15:33,133 --> 00:15:35,636
That's better than just staying in my room.

239
00:15:35,636 --> 00:15:38,906
If I stay in there any longer,
I'll get bored to death.

240
00:15:38,906 --> 00:15:41,141
That's why, still, thanks to you.

241
00:15:41,141 --> 00:15:44,144
Thank you
because you were able to convince the guards.

242
00:15:44,144 --> 00:15:45,728
That's nothing.

243
00:15:47,181 --> 00:15:49,316
You know what?

244
00:15:49,316 --> 00:15:51,914
You're a good and kind kid.

245
00:15:53,371 --> 00:15:55,961
I remember your mom carrying you.

246
00:15:59,393 --> 00:16:04,447
It seems all of you are saying
you remember Mommy carrying me.

247
00:16:05,465 --> 00:16:07,734
The truth is...

248
00:16:07,734 --> 00:16:10,854
I've been having dreams of her before.

249
00:16:28,549 --> 00:16:34,537
But I don't know if it's just a dream.

250
00:16:36,925 --> 00:16:39,410
If only she is still here.

251
00:16:40,818 --> 00:16:45,973
Maybe things will be better if she was here.

252
00:16:50,450 --> 00:16:55,716
If only she was here
to make dad understand...

253
00:16:55,716 --> 00:16:59,435
and for our family to be complete.

254
00:17:00,520 --> 00:17:02,856
No anger...

255
00:17:02,856 --> 00:17:05,241
no ill feelings.

256
00:17:06,006 --> 00:17:07,623
No fears.

257
00:17:08,320 --> 00:17:11,732
And most importantly...

258
00:17:11,732 --> 00:17:13,509
we're just happy.

259
00:17:15,369 --> 00:17:16,867
I'm sorry

260
00:17:16,868 --> 00:17:20,340
if I'm boring you
with everything I'm feeling.

261
00:17:20,340 --> 00:17:24,075
Imagine, we've only just met,

262
00:17:24,075 --> 00:17:30,717
but I'm boring you with all this
when all you wanted is to just eat.

263
00:17:30,717 --> 00:17:33,887
You know, you're really like your mom.

264
00:17:33,887 --> 00:17:36,156
She was like that too.

265
00:17:36,156 --> 00:17:40,227
She always tries to make us laugh,
even if the situation is problematic.

266
00:17:40,227 --> 00:17:42,378
She could even manage to crack some jokes.

267
00:17:46,266 --> 00:17:48,651
But remember, I told you...

268
00:17:50,086 --> 00:17:53,206
I don't like how your dad calls the shots.

269
00:17:55,142 --> 00:18:00,080
That's why I can't just watch on
while you're having a hard time.

270
00:18:00,080 --> 00:18:02,966
Because I made a promise
to your Mommy Alyanna...

271
00:18:03,917 --> 00:18:07,299
that I'll make sure
that her daughter will fine...

272
00:18:07,300 --> 00:18:09,539
and happy.

273
00:18:13,560 --> 00:18:14,711
Well...

274
00:18:15,708 --> 00:18:17,932
I can't just...

275
00:18:20,157 --> 00:18:21,942
make the decisions.

276
00:18:22,968 --> 00:18:26,440
I can't meddle with your father's decisions.

277
00:18:28,008 --> 00:18:31,127
It's you who should decide, not me.

278
00:18:32,206 --> 00:18:34,491
What do you mean?

279
00:18:39,820 --> 00:18:41,004
Baste?

280
00:18:42,155 --> 00:18:46,275
Can you please get us another juice?

281
00:18:51,531 --> 00:18:54,267
Let's go. Come on.

282
00:18:54,267 --> 00:18:55,952
Come with me.

283
00:19:03,810 --> 00:19:05,779
What's this for?

284
00:19:05,779 --> 00:19:10,550
Your dad and I call this
the secret stairs to success.

285
00:19:10,550 --> 00:19:11,918
Why?

286
00:19:11,918 --> 00:19:15,534
If you pass by these stairs,
you will become successful?

287
00:19:15,534 --> 00:19:18,611
No, these are the stairs we take...

288
00:19:18,611 --> 00:19:21,461
if you know, if we're grounded by our daddy.

289
00:19:21,461 --> 00:19:24,614
This is where we pass
so we can escape from the mansion.

290
00:19:29,002 --> 00:19:31,187
Escape from the mansion?

291
00:19:32,502 --> 00:19:33,686
Yes.

292
00:19:34,775 --> 00:19:38,861
Didn't I tell you
that only you can decide for yourself?

293
00:19:39,880 --> 00:19:42,598
If you want what your dad is doing to you...

294
00:19:43,283 --> 00:19:45,902
then go with him to America.

295
00:19:47,454 --> 00:19:49,205
But if not...

296
00:19:51,491 --> 00:19:55,244
this is your chance to escape from here.

297
00:19:56,396 --> 00:19:59,749
Or you can go back
to the parents you grew up with.

298
00:20:00,867 --> 00:20:02,919
But if you do that...

299
00:20:03,584 --> 00:20:06,336
you must not show yourself to them.

300
00:20:07,407 --> 00:20:10,893
Because for sure, your grandfather and daddy
will go looking for you.

301
00:20:14,719 --> 00:20:17,350
And if that happens,
your life will be complicated.

302
00:20:17,350 --> 00:20:18,819
Not only yours,

303
00:20:18,819 --> 00:20:21,337
but the lives
of your mother and father as well.

304
00:20:35,946 --> 00:20:38,064
Hey Nero, wait.

305
00:20:39,206 --> 00:20:40,907
Where are you going?

306
00:20:40,907 --> 00:20:43,092
I need to go out and cool down.

307
00:20:44,325 --> 00:20:46,079
What are you doing?

308
00:20:46,079 --> 00:20:47,280
I'll go with you.

309
00:20:47,280 --> 00:20:49,516
I need to cool down too.

310
00:20:49,516 --> 00:20:51,284
Can you, please?

311
00:20:51,284 --> 00:20:53,053
Just let me be alone.

312
00:20:53,053 --> 00:20:54,921
Let you be alone?

313
00:20:54,921 --> 00:20:57,224
I'm sorry, dude, but I can't do that.

314
00:20:57,224 --> 00:20:59,352
When we are alone, we tend to be impulsive

315
00:20:59,352 --> 00:21:03,029
and do stupid things
that we will regret for the rest of our lives.

316
00:21:03,029 --> 00:21:06,449
So, whether you like it or not,
I'll go with you.

317
00:21:15,675 --> 00:21:17,460
I'm sorry.

318
00:21:18,278 --> 00:21:21,230
I'm just shocked by what is happening.

319
00:21:22,749 --> 00:21:25,134
I thought everything is okay...

320
00:21:26,086 --> 00:21:29,505
But now, Florence will be far away from us.

321
00:21:31,421 --> 00:21:34,027
She will be okay, Lydia.

322
00:21:34,027 --> 00:21:40,567
I'm sure that she will find a way
to connect with you and Federico.

323
00:21:40,567 --> 00:21:41,751
You know what?

324
00:21:43,570 --> 00:21:47,423
No distance can separate a child...

325
00:21:48,070 --> 00:21:52,424
who loves the family that she knows.

326
00:21:54,047 --> 00:21:57,450
But you know, USA is still different.

327
00:21:57,450 --> 00:21:59,953
I have a friend who went to California.

328
00:21:59,953 --> 00:22:03,290
When he came back here,
he doesn't know me already.

329
00:22:03,290 --> 00:22:06,159
Hey, stop it, James.
You're making things harder.

330
00:22:06,159 --> 00:22:08,295
You know
that Lydia is going through a lot right now.

331
00:22:08,295 --> 00:22:09,679
So shut up.

332
00:22:12,766 --> 00:22:15,618
I'm not worried about that, James.

333
00:22:17,237 --> 00:22:21,708
I'm not worried if she'll forget about us,

334
00:22:21,708 --> 00:22:26,262
or if she speaks fluent English
when she comes back.

335
00:22:28,782 --> 00:22:34,904
What's bothering me
is the fact that she's so far away from us.

336
00:22:37,857 --> 00:22:41,177
What if she's all alone?

337
00:22:42,529 --> 00:22:44,647
What if she's sad?

338
00:22:47,567 --> 00:22:52,021
What if she needs someone to talk to,
or someone to lean on?

339
00:22:56,776 --> 00:23:00,930
It breaks the heart of any mother...

340
00:23:01,881 --> 00:23:05,619
if she knows that her child has no ally
or someone to depend on

341
00:23:05,621 --> 00:23:07,356
in a different country.

342
00:23:12,328 --> 00:23:15,848
Do not underestimate Florence.

343
00:23:17,864 --> 00:23:22,359
I once belittled the heart of that child.

344
00:23:25,872 --> 00:23:29,776
I thought
that she wouldn't stay long with the Ferells,

345
00:23:29,776 --> 00:23:32,679
but I was very mistaken.

346
00:23:32,679 --> 00:23:34,196
Because now...

347
00:23:35,548 --> 00:23:38,618
she has changed this house.

348
00:23:38,618 --> 00:23:44,206
And everyone is affected
by the news that she's leaving.

349
00:23:48,261 --> 00:23:50,479
You're right about that.

350
00:23:54,567 --> 00:23:56,970
I'll just tell Federico.

351
00:23:56,970 --> 00:23:58,821
As for me...

352
00:24:00,040 --> 00:24:02,575
I hope he won't feel too bad,

353
00:24:02,575 --> 00:24:04,837
because his heart might not be able
to handle it.

354
00:24:05,812 --> 00:24:07,480
Wait...

355
00:24:07,480 --> 00:24:12,452
Where are Federico, Dencio, and Iking?

356
00:24:12,452 --> 00:24:15,738
How come I haven't seen them
for quite some time?

357
00:24:22,629 --> 00:24:25,565
Are you sure where we're going?

358
00:24:25,565 --> 00:24:28,184
We're getting lost already.

359
00:24:30,837 --> 00:24:34,123
Don't pressure me. That was 17 years ago.

360
00:24:34,924 --> 00:24:36,170
Wait.

361
00:24:37,143 --> 00:24:38,445
I remember something.

362
00:24:38,445 --> 00:24:40,113
There. Wait, hold on.

363
00:24:40,113 --> 00:24:41,630
- Okay, go.
- Yes, that's right.

364
00:24:41,630 --> 00:24:43,850
Okay, okay.

365
00:24:43,850 --> 00:24:46,019
Wait, wait. Okay.

366
00:24:46,019 --> 00:24:47,587
- Okay, go.
- What now?

367
00:24:47,587 --> 00:24:49,872
- Okay.
- There's a delicious Bulaluhan here.

368
00:24:50,890 --> 00:24:52,425
- Over there.
- Really?

369
00:24:52,425 --> 00:24:53,993
Yes. Let's go there.

370
00:24:53,993 --> 00:24:56,534
Good thing you remembered something, somehow.

371
00:24:56,534 --> 00:24:58,063
That's a good start.

372
00:24:58,064 --> 00:25:00,516
- Ouch.
- Let's go. Hurry.

373
00:25:03,136 --> 00:25:06,439
It seems this field trip of ours is useless.

374
00:25:06,439 --> 00:25:08,908
I can't remember anything.

375
00:25:08,908 --> 00:25:10,510
Just relax.

376
00:25:10,510 --> 00:25:15,264
Buddy, remember, we have a saying
that virtue is a patience.

377
00:25:16,015 --> 00:25:18,318
That's right.

378
00:25:18,318 --> 00:25:20,854
Virtue is a patience.

379
00:25:20,854 --> 00:25:22,938
And this is a good idea.

380
00:25:24,023 --> 00:25:25,291
Who knows?

381
00:25:25,291 --> 00:25:29,111
Once you've tasted
the delicious beef soup here...

382
00:25:29,829 --> 00:25:33,199
it will trigger again your old memory

383
00:25:33,199 --> 00:25:36,035
that is sleeping in your subconscious.

384
00:25:36,035 --> 00:25:37,404
You know what?

385
00:25:37,404 --> 00:25:39,155
Iking, you know a lot of things.

386
00:25:41,241 --> 00:25:45,867
Well, being prompt beats being diligent,

387
00:25:45,868 --> 00:25:53,202
but a person who is wise
beats the diligent and prompt person.

388
00:25:54,254 --> 00:25:55,655
That's a nice quote.

389
00:25:55,655 --> 00:25:57,457
Wow, that's possible.

390
00:25:57,457 --> 00:25:59,292
Here it is.

391
00:25:59,292 --> 00:26:00,776
There, there...

392
00:26:02,195 --> 00:26:04,413
Yes, this is delicious.

393
00:26:06,232 --> 00:26:09,502
More brains, more chances of winning.

394
00:26:09,502 --> 00:26:12,705
More brains, more power.

395
00:26:12,705 --> 00:26:14,641
Wait. Wait for a second.

396
00:26:14,641 --> 00:26:18,745
Waitress, this includes...

397
00:26:18,745 --> 00:26:20,880
- Salsa.
- Salsa.

398
00:26:20,880 --> 00:26:22,882
We've run out of salsa, Sir.

399
00:26:22,882 --> 00:26:24,818
- There's no more salsa.
- Yes.

400
00:26:24,818 --> 00:26:26,494
There's a different salsa I know.

401
00:26:26,494 --> 00:26:29,647
Yes, go ahead and show them.

402
00:26:30,690 --> 00:26:36,126
- Salsa, salsa.
- Salsa, baby.

403
00:26:39,232 --> 00:26:41,134
Federico, salsa.

404
00:26:41,134 --> 00:26:43,570
Just relax, buddy,
and for sure you'll remember it.

405
00:26:43,570 --> 00:26:46,105
- Go on. Think harder.
- Stop it.

406
00:26:46,105 --> 00:26:47,574
He's hungry already.

407
00:26:47,574 --> 00:26:50,893
<i>♪ Federico ♪</i>

408
00:26:51,611 --> 00:26:54,864
<i>♪ Salsa, salsa ♪</i>

409
00:26:54,864 --> 00:26:58,885
<i>♪ Federico ♪</i>

410
00:26:58,885 --> 00:27:00,787
<i>♪ Salsa ♪</i>

411
00:27:00,787 --> 00:27:02,171
<i>♪ Salsa ♪</i>

412
00:27:03,223 --> 00:27:04,891
Look...

413
00:27:04,891 --> 00:27:09,429
I do not profess
that I understand what you're feeling.

414
00:27:09,429 --> 00:27:14,033
A part of me is jealous
that you found someone like Florence.

415
00:27:14,033 --> 00:27:19,239
A part of me is also relieved
that I'm not going through your struggles.

416
00:27:19,239 --> 00:27:23,543
That's why I'm not in the position
to give advice.

417
00:27:23,543 --> 00:27:26,679
But being the eldest among us five...

418
00:27:26,679 --> 00:27:28,330
allow me to try.

419
00:27:30,250 --> 00:27:32,368
I don't need your help.

420
00:27:33,788 --> 00:27:36,523
Unless you help me get inside
the mansion of the Almeros,

421
00:27:36,523 --> 00:27:38,791
to get Florence.

422
00:27:38,791 --> 00:27:39,926
And then what?

423
00:27:39,926 --> 00:27:42,778
You'll elope
and you'll live happily ever after?

424
00:27:46,466 --> 00:27:48,368
Whatever.

425
00:27:48,368 --> 00:27:50,352
As long as we're together.

426
00:27:53,473 --> 00:27:54,990
It's romantic...

427
00:27:56,009 --> 00:27:59,646
your idea of just running away.

428
00:27:59,646 --> 00:28:04,644
But sometimes, we need to face the truth...

429
00:28:04,644 --> 00:28:09,164
that you and Florence bring out
a lot of complications.

430
00:28:10,623 --> 00:28:12,408
At the end of the day...

431
00:28:13,793 --> 00:28:15,277
you're a Ferell.

432
00:28:18,031 --> 00:28:20,049
And she's an Almero.

433
00:28:24,037 --> 00:28:25,554
Stop the car.

434
00:28:27,373 --> 00:28:29,358
Hey, Nero! Where are you going?

435
00:28:32,078 --> 00:28:33,429
Florence?

436
00:28:34,914 --> 00:28:36,124
What's happening?

437
00:28:36,124 --> 00:28:38,042
I saw Florence.

438
00:28:39,085 --> 00:28:40,820
Maybe your eyes are just
playing tricks on you.

439
00:28:40,820 --> 00:28:43,539
I can't make a mistake.
I really saw her face.

440
00:28:44,714 --> 00:28:46,559
There's nothing.

441
00:28:46,559 --> 00:28:47,943
Let's go.

442
00:28:51,879 --> 00:28:53,029
Let's go.

443
00:28:54,470 --> 00:28:55,821
Nero?

444
00:29:10,203 --> 00:29:13,206
He is tall, just like Dingdong Dantes.

445
00:29:13,953 --> 00:29:16,623
Let's focus on the face. Face.

446
00:29:16,623 --> 00:29:19,069
He has a long face...

447
00:29:19,069 --> 00:29:23,663
and his eyes are deep set, like that.

448
00:29:23,663 --> 00:29:25,965
And this, I remember.

449
00:29:25,965 --> 00:29:28,384
He has a mole on his nose.

450
00:29:29,435 --> 00:29:30,503
What, Iking?

451
00:29:30,503 --> 00:29:31,771
Did you get it?

452
00:29:31,771 --> 00:29:36,098
Maybe that's another cartoon character.

453
00:29:36,098 --> 00:29:38,484
No. This time, it's for real.

454
00:29:38,484 --> 00:29:41,864
- Look, this is a real person.
- Let me see.

455
00:29:43,736 --> 00:29:45,320
Federico, look at this.

456
00:29:47,811 --> 00:29:49,329
This is the one.

457
00:29:50,095 --> 00:29:53,292
He's the man I saw. I'm sure.

458
00:29:53,292 --> 00:29:54,917
Who is that?

459
00:29:57,378 --> 00:30:00,564
I think I saw him around when it was 4:30 PM.

460
00:30:02,808 --> 00:30:04,792
Gio Alvarez.

461
00:30:09,294 --> 00:30:11,321
I beg to disagree.

462
00:30:11,321 --> 00:30:13,312
Let me see, buddy.

463
00:30:13,312 --> 00:30:14,673
Gio Alvarez?

464
00:30:14,673 --> 00:30:18,351
No, Iking, this looks like Bobby Andrews,

465
00:30:18,351 --> 00:30:19,986
the guy in TGIS.

466
00:30:19,986 --> 00:30:21,704
Yes, that's TGIS.

467
00:30:22,897 --> 00:30:26,008
Right? The one from TGIS.

468
00:30:27,571 --> 00:30:30,396
Why do you have a drawing of Mr. Samuel?

469
00:30:30,396 --> 00:30:32,109
- Samuel?
- Samuel?

470
00:30:32,933 --> 00:30:34,432
Do you know this person?

471
00:30:34,432 --> 00:30:35,902
Yes, he often comes here.

472
00:30:35,902 --> 00:30:39,054
That's Mr. Samuel. Samuel Almero.

473
00:30:46,696 --> 00:30:48,381
Celestina?

474
00:30:52,652 --> 00:30:54,170
Celestina?

475
00:30:58,325 --> 00:30:59,942
Celestina?

476
00:31:14,941 --> 00:31:17,144
I'm sorry, Nero, but I need to go.

477
00:31:17,144 --> 00:31:20,032
And besides, no one should see us together.

478
00:31:20,032 --> 00:31:24,003
So just go home to the mansion,
and don't tell anyone that you saw me.

479
00:31:24,003 --> 00:31:26,498
And you too, Tristan.

480
00:31:26,498 --> 00:31:28,690
Wait, what are you talking about?

481
00:31:31,197 --> 00:31:35,384
I'll go to a faraway place, Nero...

482
00:31:36,038 --> 00:31:37,922
all by myself.

483
00:31:39,451 --> 00:31:41,135
Well, I'll go with you.

484
00:31:41,754 --> 00:31:44,557
Nero, I already told you
that it's not possible.

485
00:31:44,557 --> 00:31:46,659
You'll only get involved.

486
00:31:46,659 --> 00:31:49,862
Everyone will be involved
with my problem now.

487
00:31:49,862 --> 00:31:52,681
And things will be more complicated.

488
00:31:54,100 --> 00:31:55,689
Florence...

489
00:31:55,689 --> 00:31:58,271
I am involved in everything
that will happen to you...

490
00:31:58,271 --> 00:31:59,872
when I chose you.

491
00:31:59,872 --> 00:32:02,057
When I decided to love you...

492
00:32:02,875 --> 00:32:05,160
I've already accepted all your complications.

493
00:32:06,078 --> 00:32:08,063
Nero, please.

494
00:32:09,749 --> 00:32:11,617
I'm sorry, Florence...

495
00:32:11,617 --> 00:32:13,669
but I will never leave your side.

496
00:32:14,387 --> 00:32:16,455
Call me irrational...

497
00:32:16,455 --> 00:32:21,193
but others are saying
that I'm a hopeless romantic.

498
00:32:21,193 --> 00:32:23,362
But what's wrong with that?

499
00:32:23,362 --> 00:32:25,398
What's wrong with being stupid?

500
00:32:25,398 --> 00:32:27,716
What's wrong with losing everything...

501
00:32:28,826 --> 00:32:31,578
if I'm with the person I love so much?

502
00:32:37,393 --> 00:32:39,011
I'm sorry, Florence...

503
00:32:40,609 --> 00:32:42,994
but I will never leave your side.

504
00:32:44,034 --> 00:32:46,018
I will never leave you...

505
00:32:46,953 --> 00:32:49,037
whether you like it or not.

506
00:32:55,602 --> 00:32:57,232
- How about her clothes in the room?
- Celestina?

507
00:32:57,232 --> 00:32:59,732
- Is it still there?
- Celestina!

508
00:32:59,732 --> 00:33:02,668
Celestina! Dad, where is she?

509
00:33:02,668 --> 00:33:04,103
Celestina is missing.

510
00:33:04,103 --> 00:33:07,440
Calm down. I've already asked our guards
to look for her.

511
00:33:07,440 --> 00:33:09,508
Dad, Celestina is missing.

512
00:33:09,508 --> 00:33:11,444
We've checked every corner of the mansion,

513
00:33:11,444 --> 00:33:12,979
but Miss Florence is no longer around.

514
00:33:12,979 --> 00:33:14,963
I mean Celestina.

515
00:33:16,282 --> 00:33:18,084
Where is Celestina?

516
00:33:18,084 --> 00:33:21,921
Dad, look, how can I calm down?
My daughter is missing again!

517
00:33:21,921 --> 00:33:24,590
This is all your fault, Lorenzo...

518
00:33:24,590 --> 00:33:27,293
You're the reason why Florence is rebelling.

519
00:33:27,293 --> 00:33:29,295
Her name is Celestina.

520
00:33:29,295 --> 00:33:31,597
And what do you know about being a father?

521
00:33:31,597 --> 00:33:34,100
Don't interfere with family matters.

522
00:33:34,100 --> 00:33:36,889
Calm down, that's enough.

523
00:33:36,889 --> 00:33:38,331
Choose your words, Lorenzo.

524
00:33:38,331 --> 00:33:40,339
Your anger won't help right now.

525
00:33:40,339 --> 00:33:45,661
What's important is we have to figure out
where Florence went.

526
00:33:49,715 --> 00:33:52,167
I think I have an idea where she went.

527
00:33:56,622 --> 00:33:58,427
So, this is your plan?

528
00:33:58,427 --> 00:34:01,627
For both of you to leave
and go to a faraway place?

529
00:34:01,627 --> 00:34:04,130
I won't go back to the mansion.

530
00:34:04,130 --> 00:34:06,498
I don't want to go to the States.

531
00:34:06,498 --> 00:34:09,984
I won't allow them to just force me
to do what they want.

532
00:34:11,237 --> 00:34:13,821
So, you'll both go to a faraway place?

533
00:34:13,821 --> 00:34:15,341
Why not?

534
00:34:15,341 --> 00:34:16,509
What do you mean why not?

535
00:34:16,509 --> 00:34:18,460
You won't survive.

536
00:34:20,406 --> 00:34:22,691
I know how to cook.

537
00:34:23,516 --> 00:34:25,967
I can sell food again.

538
00:34:28,220 --> 00:34:31,624
I can work as a fish porter in the market.

539
00:34:31,624 --> 00:34:35,277
Or let's just go back to the mansion?

540
00:34:51,343 --> 00:34:54,180
No, that's not possible.

541
00:34:54,180 --> 00:34:56,682
I don't want to go back to Mother and Father.

542
00:34:56,682 --> 00:35:00,335
If the Almeros find out,
they'll be dragged into this again.

543
00:35:02,154 --> 00:35:05,273
I don't want Grandpa Garp's situation
to be complicated.

544
00:35:06,092 --> 00:35:09,495
That might spell more problems
with the Almeros.

545
00:35:09,495 --> 00:35:13,348
Do you think the Almeros won't find you?

546
00:35:19,105 --> 00:35:23,892
What if we change our names?

547
00:35:25,044 --> 00:35:26,795
I'll be Sophia.

548
00:35:30,563 --> 00:35:31,981
And I'll be Allen.

549
00:35:33,119 --> 00:35:34,954
Hey, this is serious.

550
00:35:34,954 --> 00:35:36,972
You guys cannot do this alone.

551
00:35:38,090 --> 00:35:40,842
Don't decide impulsively.

552
00:35:41,627 --> 00:35:46,432
At the very least,
let's talk to our friends first.

553
00:35:46,432 --> 00:35:47,867
If not me,

554
00:35:47,867 --> 00:35:51,253
it'll be them who'll be able to
talk sense to the both of you.

555
00:35:57,877 --> 00:35:59,294
Go ahead and board.

556
00:36:00,980 --> 00:36:02,697
Just move.

557
00:36:03,365 --> 00:36:05,417
And your payment, please.

558
00:36:09,155 --> 00:36:13,125
Guys, let's just take it easy.

559
00:36:13,125 --> 00:36:15,461
We'll be dealing with the Almeros.

560
00:36:15,461 --> 00:36:17,129
If we take a swipe,

561
00:36:17,129 --> 00:36:19,155
we have to be sure that it's a bullseye.

562
00:36:19,155 --> 00:36:23,819
Because if not,
this will all land on our faces.

563
00:36:26,572 --> 00:36:29,808
What evidence do we need to prove

564
00:36:29,808 --> 00:36:35,724
that Samuel has nothing to do
with Florence and Alyanna?

565
00:36:35,724 --> 00:36:38,877
Why was he at the scene of the crime?

566
00:36:40,202 --> 00:36:42,921
All I'm thinking about is Florence right now.

567
00:36:45,257 --> 00:36:47,699
It's like my heart will explode

568
00:36:47,699 --> 00:36:52,364
whenever I'm thinking that she's staying
with a murderer in the same house.

569
00:36:52,364 --> 00:36:54,300
Don't worry.

570
00:36:54,300 --> 00:36:59,554
I'm sure Grandpa Garp will do everything
to protect Florence.

571
00:37:01,373 --> 00:37:02,757
Thank you.

572
00:37:04,910 --> 00:37:07,662
I hope nothing bad will happen to Florence.

573
00:37:08,514 --> 00:37:13,101
Because if not, all hell will break lose.

574
00:37:14,120 --> 00:37:16,338
I will make them pay.

575
00:37:24,830 --> 00:37:26,899
Celestina?

576
00:37:26,899 --> 00:37:28,767
Celestina?

577
00:37:28,767 --> 00:37:30,485
Come out now.

578
00:37:37,427 --> 00:37:40,112
What are you doing here?

579
00:37:40,112 --> 00:37:42,097
Where is Celestina?

580
00:37:42,881 --> 00:37:44,316
Florence is not here.

581
00:37:44,316 --> 00:37:46,919
Just cut to the chase, Mr. Garpidio.

582
00:37:46,919 --> 00:37:48,187
This is the only place where she can go,

583
00:37:48,187 --> 00:37:50,205
that's why I know you're hiding her.

584
00:37:50,856 --> 00:37:52,908
You are wrong, Lorenzo.

585
00:37:54,493 --> 00:37:58,342
Maybe instead of asking if Florence is here,

586
00:37:58,342 --> 00:38:03,535
you should ask yourselves
why she ran away from you.

587
00:38:03,535 --> 00:38:05,704
Please, Mrs. Dela Cruz.

588
00:38:05,704 --> 00:38:07,373
Don't meddle here.

589
00:38:07,373 --> 00:38:08,890
Why not?

590
00:38:13,545 --> 00:38:16,498
You took my daughter from me.

591
00:38:17,773 --> 00:38:21,360
And now that she's missing,
you're still looking for her here?

592
00:38:23,722 --> 00:38:25,573
All my life...

593
00:38:26,492 --> 00:38:29,978
that girl never left my sight.

594
00:38:31,830 --> 00:38:36,988
All my life, I know where she is.

595
00:38:36,988 --> 00:38:40,639
Where she sleeps, and what time she wakes up.

596
00:38:40,639 --> 00:38:44,693
And now she's missing,
you're looking for her here?

597
00:38:50,849 --> 00:38:53,368
We were living a quiet life.

598
00:38:55,220 --> 00:39:00,392
And then you came and told us
that you're her real family?

599
00:39:00,392 --> 00:39:02,027
You should be ashamed.

600
00:39:02,027 --> 00:39:04,813
You're so thick-skinned.

601
00:39:08,834 --> 00:39:10,803
If there's something I know about Florence,

602
00:39:10,803 --> 00:39:12,538
it's that she'll never leave your side

603
00:39:12,538 --> 00:39:16,358
if she knows and feels real love from you.

604
00:39:21,836 --> 00:39:23,454
I just hope...

605
00:39:26,719 --> 00:39:29,623
I do hope Florence is here.

606
00:39:29,623 --> 00:39:32,475
I hope she went back to our house...

607
00:39:35,908 --> 00:39:39,905
Because if that happens,
I will never give her back to you,

608
00:39:39,905 --> 00:39:42,190
even if you kill me.

609
00:39:43,802 --> 00:39:45,954
You can never get my daughter back.

610
00:39:54,848 --> 00:39:56,032
Guys?

611
00:39:57,643 --> 00:39:59,327
- It's Florence.
- Florence.

612
00:40:00,295 --> 00:40:02,991
What are you doing?

613
00:40:02,991 --> 00:40:05,276
- Are you okay?
- Where have you been?

614
00:40:06,794 --> 00:40:10,729
We went to Antonia when we learned
that you have an issue in the mansion.

615
00:40:10,729 --> 00:40:12,698
We wanted to know more details.

616
00:40:12,698 --> 00:40:13,566
See?

617
00:40:13,567 --> 00:40:16,000
We were just talking about you,
and all of a sudden you're here already.

618
00:40:17,148 --> 00:40:20,505
I'm so sorry, Florence, this is all my fault.

619
00:40:20,506 --> 00:40:23,242
I was so eager to post on my account.

620
00:40:23,242 --> 00:40:24,476
I'm sorry.

621
00:40:24,476 --> 00:40:27,379
Camille, don't apologize.
It's not your fault.

622
00:40:27,379 --> 00:40:31,059
Don't stop yourself
just because other people have issues.

623
00:40:31,059 --> 00:40:33,688
Still, she could've been more careful.

624
00:40:33,688 --> 00:40:36,139
A little bit of sensitivity can go a long way.

625
00:40:36,139 --> 00:40:39,305
She knows the issue
between the Almeros and Ferells.

626
00:40:39,305 --> 00:40:43,008
When I heard that her dad showed that post,

627
00:40:43,008 --> 00:40:45,311
I already sensed that you'll be in trouble,

628
00:40:45,311 --> 00:40:48,947
especially when Antonia told us
about your dad's request

629
00:40:48,947 --> 00:40:51,884
to fix your travel documents.

630
00:40:51,884 --> 00:40:56,088
But, we didn't expect
that his reaction would be that big.

631
00:40:56,088 --> 00:40:58,424
I mean, really?

632
00:40:58,424 --> 00:41:01,560
Will they actually pull you out of Gyronella?

633
00:41:01,560 --> 00:41:05,297
Even worse, live and go to school abroad?

634
00:41:05,297 --> 00:41:09,919
Believe me, Antonia,
I don't agree with their decision,

635
00:41:09,919 --> 00:41:12,304
but it's also coming from a good place.

636
00:41:12,304 --> 00:41:14,606
Wait, but why do you look that way?

637
00:41:14,606 --> 00:41:15,808
You don't look like an Almero.

638
00:41:15,808 --> 00:41:18,493
You look like a criminal
hiding from the authorities.

639
00:41:19,511 --> 00:41:22,163
It looks like you also don't agree
with your father's decision.

640
00:41:24,395 --> 00:41:26,452
The reason why I brought them here,

641
00:41:26,452 --> 00:41:28,721
is because I told them
to talk about their plan.

642
00:41:28,721 --> 00:41:30,723
- Plan?
- What plan?

643
00:41:30,723 --> 00:41:33,341
They plan to be impulsive and stupid.

644
00:41:34,326 --> 00:41:36,795
We plan to go to a faraway place.

645
00:41:36,795 --> 00:41:39,698
To elope and live together.

646
00:41:39,698 --> 00:41:41,680
Away from all these problems.

647
00:41:42,635 --> 00:41:44,322
What?

648
00:41:45,402 --> 00:41:47,440
OMG!

649
00:41:48,543 --> 00:41:50,167
Wow!

650
00:41:51,643 --> 00:41:55,948
Maybe we can all calm down.

651
00:41:55,948 --> 00:41:59,318
I know the emotions you are feeling now
are intense.

652
00:41:59,318 --> 00:42:01,987
We all have ill feelings...

653
00:42:01,987 --> 00:42:03,772
that come from them.

654
00:42:04,702 --> 00:42:06,959
Maybe you have forgotten.

655
00:42:06,959 --> 00:42:09,015
Florence is still missing.

656
00:42:09,015 --> 00:42:12,564
It's better if we look for her first
before you nag at each other.

657
00:42:12,564 --> 00:42:13,699
You animal!

658
00:42:13,699 --> 00:42:17,803
- You're an animal! Animal!
- Federico, calm down.

659
00:42:17,803 --> 00:42:19,939
Let go of me. I'll kill that animal!

660
00:42:19,939 --> 00:42:23,835
- Federico!
- Federico! Don't be impulsive!

661
00:42:23,835 --> 00:42:26,645
How dare you attack my son!

662
00:42:26,645 --> 00:42:28,847
How dare me attack your son?

663
00:42:28,847 --> 00:42:30,616
You shouldn't be saying that to me.

664
00:42:30,616 --> 00:42:33,519
You should say that to this animal, your son!

665
00:42:33,519 --> 00:42:36,221
Wait, how did you know each other?

666
00:42:36,221 --> 00:42:38,190
We don't know each other.

667
00:42:38,190 --> 00:42:42,227
But that face... I remember that face!

668
00:42:42,227 --> 00:42:45,330
He killed your wife, Alyanna.

669
00:42:45,330 --> 00:42:48,600
And he is the reason
why Florence ended with us.

670
00:42:48,600 --> 00:42:51,370
- Federico...
- Calm down, Federico.

671
00:42:51,370 --> 00:42:54,327
That is a very serious accusation.

672
00:42:54,327 --> 00:42:58,076
Do you have any evidence
to accuse us of that crime?

673
00:42:58,076 --> 00:42:59,478
I was there.

674
00:42:59,478 --> 00:43:02,648
I was there in the area
where Alyanna was killed.

675
00:43:35,505 --> 00:43:37,523
I'm sorry, Celestina.

676
00:43:38,762 --> 00:43:41,013
Mommy has to go.

677
00:43:42,554 --> 00:43:44,639
Just stay here first.

678
00:43:48,995 --> 00:43:52,702
I love you so much.

679
00:43:52,702 --> 00:43:54,414
I love you...

680
00:44:02,545 --> 00:44:04,453
I love you.

681
00:44:07,145 --> 00:44:09,697
I love you, Celestina.

682
00:44:25,531 --> 00:44:30,669
Maybe Alyanna escaped from you that night.

683
00:44:30,669 --> 00:44:33,171
She knew the situation was dangerous,
that's why she couldn't do anything,

684
00:44:33,171 --> 00:44:35,679
but protect her daughter!

685
00:44:45,017 --> 00:44:48,487
Wait, where is the hospital
you're talking about?

686
00:44:48,487 --> 00:44:50,713
Over there. It's Mary Grace Hospital.

687
00:44:50,713 --> 00:44:54,927
Wait, we're not going there.
This is going out of Levante.

688
00:44:54,927 --> 00:44:57,663
- Get down.
- Uncle Samuel, why do you have that?

689
00:44:57,663 --> 00:44:59,798
Don't ask too many questions. Get down!

690
00:44:59,798 --> 00:45:02,000
Why are you doing this?

691
00:45:02,000 --> 00:45:05,938
Florence, I just need you, so I can escape.

692
00:45:05,938 --> 00:45:09,090
So I can get money from your grandpa
and your daddy...

693
00:45:09,908 --> 00:45:14,680
because I wanted to start again,
and stay away from you.

694
00:45:14,680 --> 00:45:16,573
You will pay for all your sins.

695
00:45:16,573 --> 00:45:17,765
Why?

696
00:45:18,650 --> 00:45:21,048
What do you know about my sins?
